===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|rennet}}, from {{inh|en|ang|*rynnet}}, {{m|ang|*ġerynnet}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*garunniþu|t=coagulation, curdling, rennet}}, cognate with {{cog|osx|girunnida|t=a running together, coagulation}}, {{cog|goh|girunnida|t=rennet, coagulation}}, {{cog|gmh|gerinnede|t=that which is curdled}}. 

Compare also {{cog|enm|renelesse}}, {{m|enm|renels}}, {{m|enm|renlys}}, {{m|enm|rendlys|t=rennet}}, {{cog|dum|rinsel}}, {{m|dum|runsel|t=rennet}}, {{cog|enm|irennen|t=to curdle; to run}}, {{cog|ang|ġerennan|t=to coagulate}}, {{cog|goh|girunst|t=rennet}}, {{cog|de|gerinnen|t=to coagulate; congeal}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|runnet}} {{qualifier|dialectal}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}
{{wikipedia}}

# An [[enzyme]] used as the first step in making [[cheese]], to [[curdle]] the milk and [[coagulate]] the [[casein]] in it, derived by soaking the fourth [[stomach]] of a milk-fed [[calf]] in [[brine]].

